  "id": "cyclic-adenosine-monophosphate",
  "term": "cyclic adenosine monophosphate",
  "definition": "Cyclic adenosine monophosphate (cAMP) is a signaling molecule made from adenosine triphosphate that acts as a second messenger inside cells, helping transmit cellular responses. In the psychology-related research described here, lower cAMP levels were reported in some studies of major depressive disorder and were discussed as a state-related biological finding linked to reduced metabolism.",
